commit cb98a42817095c3097c63493ba2830ba8cb8a8a2

C03: a countdown answer need not restate the observed clock (CLOCK1331)

CLOCK1329 measured: «Faltan 14 horas y 7 minutos para las 3 de la tarde.» was the correct countdown answer, but the clock fact check demanded the observed time in the text and vetoed it eighteen times (missing_name). With countdown facts in the payload the observed clock is optional in the final; a contrary clock claim is still a defect, and the instruction asks for the remaining time until the target, with the clock as an option.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


